    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1129">

                <pb facs="0938" n="822" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg822"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/4500.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                            American Ambassador</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-07-29T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 29, 1912—4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Lay Department’s July 28, midnight, before American Consul at Chihuahua; instruct
                    him to send Department his recommendations as soon as possible, and to do all he
                    can to alleviate situation in rebel territory. See Department’s March 2, 2 p.m.,
                    and telegraph your recommendations concerning advisability of Americans leaving
                    their present residences.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Knox.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
